# render
- label: rendered session Playwright coverage verifies keyboard navigation, native filter activation, and accessible state updates in a real rendered session viewer
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'rendered session keyboard' test/browser/rendered-session-keyboard.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, rendered-session, playwright, accessibility, implemented]

# server
- label: tracequest serve refreshes served root HTML after a nested browser helper edit in a real subprocess: the source watcher sends reload SSE, modVersion invalidates route output, and the next / response includes the edited helper output
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'nested browser helper edit refreshes served root HTML after reload' test/bin/tracequest-livereload-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, server-hot-reload, implemented]

# features

## live
- label: the serve API populates liveSessions from the full unfiltered session snapshot and the browser refresh path updates the pinned unified live rows and row badge set from each /api/sessions response
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/bin/tracequest-serve-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-ui, implemented]
- label: served browser tests load tracequest serve in Playwright and verify an external live session renders as ONE unified live row (run-row chrome, running state badge, external origin chip, /run?session=<hash> click target, no #liveBar strip, no duplicate session row) from the initial page payload and after window._refreshData fetches /api/sessions
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/browser/live-ui-served.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-ui, browser-live, implemented]
- label: served browser tests verify a real data-update SSE event from tracequest serve, triggered by writing a watched session file, causes the open browser page to fetch /api/sessions and render the new session without directly calling window._refreshData
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'data-update SSE refreshes the open page without direct refresh invocation' test/browser/live-ui-served.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, live-ui, browser-live, serve-refresh, implemented]

